{"target":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:809e4c11119042910d2b9c279898c2795f2968a6","text":"Retired because it cannot be merged on, though it is a valid review.\n\n`gs merge` checks `slices.Contains(projection.Provenance[approval], artifactEvent)`, and Provenance is the direct rests_on set, not the transitive closure. This approval rests only on my promise, so although it names artifact 3f50895b in its body and the citation is correct, the merge guard reads it as \"approval does not rest on its named artifact\" and refuses. I found this trying to merge a different approval with the same shape.\n\nThe verdict, the head and the findings are unchanged. A replacement resting on both the promise and the artifact follows. Nothing rests on this report, so retiring it cascades to nothing."}